Season 23 , episode 1
It's an all-new season of The Amazing Race, and we're starting off the first leg at an old Western movie ranch. Before we get started, though, let's meet the duos:
Chester and Ephraim, an NFL duo;
Rowan and Shane, theatre performers from North Carolina;
Tim and Marie, exes (and friends) from New Jersey;
Leo and Jamal, cousins from California who refer to themselves as the "Afghanimals" (because they're Afghan and animals, if you missed that);
Ally and Ashley, NHL ice crew teammates;
Nicole and Travis, married ER physicians from Atlanta;
Hoskote and Naina, father and daughter;
Tim and Dan, oil plant workers from Oklahoma;
Brandon and Adam, childhood friends from Chico, California (this year's rockers!);
Nicky and Kim, major league baseball wives from the midwest;
Jason and Amy, a dating couple from New England.
The group meets Phil Keoghan for their intro, where they're told they'll be traveling first to the coastline of South America. Whoever wins the first leg of the race will get an Express Pass - plus an additional one to hand over to another team by the fifth leg. The first clue is just a phone call away, so they'll get ready to head to one of the nearby Ford hybrids (product placement!) to make a call to the other side of the world for it. And off they go!
