The clue is to head to LAX to get to Inquique, Chile - but guess what? There's only a limited amount of seats on the first flight, so they'll need to hurry. Once they get there, they'll need to go look for Javier, the guy on the other end of the line giving them their first clue.
Tim & Danny aren't off to such a good start, as they get lost and try to ask a woman who doesn't speak English for directions. Leo & Jamal fare slightly better, though, as they're first on the American Airlines flight that'll get into Chile first. Chester & Ephram are right behind them, followed by Rowan & Shane. Tim & Marie, Ashley & Ally, Nicky & Kim and Nicole & Travis round out the first flight. That leaves the rest of the teams on the second flight. Not such a good start! Ally & Ashley and Leo & Jamal form an alliance in the waiting room, by the way - though it's a bit early for that and it probably won't last.
In Inquique, teams will need to travel by taxi to Alto Hospicio, where they'll need to search for the Zona de Parapetes and Javier will hand them their next clue. Nicole & Travis get the first taxi, but can they get to Alto Hospicio first? Yep! It's a Roadblock, which requires one person from each team to follow their partner as they paraglide down the rocky cliffs. Once they're reunited on the beach, they'll get their next clue.
© CBS Robert Voets
Nicole & Travis have got a great advantage in Nicole's ability to speak Spanish. It allows her to communicate with her taxi driver and let him know that she needs to go meet her husband on the beach when he lands. However, several of the teams are in the air are the same time, so it's not necessarily a surefire victory for them. In fact, somehow Rowan & Shane slip into first place, where they discover that they'll need to head to Muelle Prat for their next clue. Nicole & Travis are right behind them, though, followed closely by our football players.
At Muelle Prat, there's another Roadblock which requires teams to choose a rowboat and search Inquique's harbor to collect a total of five fish from any of three fishing boats, each containing a limited number of fish. Once delivered to the fishmonger, they'll be handed their next clue. Travis heads off on his own to do it - it looks pretty difficult.
Nicole & Travis regain their first place position as they finish the Roadblock first, receiving the next clue, which instructs them to head to this week's Pit Stop at Teatro Municipal de Inquique, a national monument. The first team gets those Express Passes, in case you forgot, while the last time to check in will be eliminated.
© CBS Robert Voets
Nicole & Travis do indeed arrive first, but since they didn't read their clue (which states that they needed to make their way to the Pit Stop by foot), they've got a 30-minute penalty. They could still come in first, but we'll have to see. Unfortunately, Tim & Marie get there before that penalty is up and win the Express Passes. Aw, bad luck. They at least come in second and are safe.
The rest of the teams come trickling in little by little, but unfortunately, it's Hoskote and Naina who turn up last and are eliminated from the race. They're disappointed - in fact, Naina is "devastated" - but ah, that's just how it goes, I suppose.
Tune in to CBS on Sunday, October 6 at 8/7c to find out where the teams will head next!
